    {
      "id": "2DNuqfBhWSrzXko8y8buW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80.28358556138971,
      "y": 18359.804170409374,
      "width": 1145.86669921875,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "us3J9UXm3Lo2_ybWADzz-",
        "iawWWCZovYvlboldb0hq2",
        "KYDunAKVG9xsZIgBFzSG7"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0Ab",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1377635923,
      "version": 480,
      "versionNonce": 1499534812,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793701873306,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--> LLM inference consists of 2 fundamentally different phases : \n\n            ° Prefill \n\n    and \n\n            ° Decode",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> LLM inference consists of 2 fundamentally different phases : \n\n            ° Prefill \n\n    and \n\n            ° Decode",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1793530194714,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "AnHWyc0oo5wPS7lBU4Mp3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.28358556138971,
      "y": 18779.804170409374,
      "width": 1612.38330078125,
      "height": 1125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "Ds1hvPaaBYN_q9IDC1y11",
        "iawWWCZovYvlboldb0hq2",
        "KYDunAKVG9xsZIgBFzSG7"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0Ac",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1856883699,
      "version": 684,
      "versionNonce": 961070564,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793701873306,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--> Prefill Phase ( Prompt Processing ) :\n\n        ° Computes K and V for ALL input tokens,\n\n        ° Stores both in Cache\n\n        ° The intermediate states Keys and Values are used to Generate the FIRST Token\n\n\n        ° Processes all input tokens in parallel\n\n        ° Compute-intensive with high GPU utilization\n\n        ° Generates initial KV cache entries for all prompt tokens\n\n        ° Latency proportional to prompt length\n\n        ° Benefits from larger batch sizes\n\n\n        ==>  Each new token depends on all the previous tokens, but because the full extent\n              of the input is known, at a high level this is a matrix-matrix operation that’s \n              highly parallelized.\n\n        ==> It effectively saturates GPU utilization",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> Prefill Phase ( Prompt Processing ) :\n\n        ° Computes K and V for ALL input tokens,\n\n        ° Stores both in Cache\n\n        ° The intermediate states Keys and Values are used to Generate the FIRST Token\n\n\n        ° Processes all input tokens in parallel\n\n        ° Compute-intensive with high GPU utilization\n\n        ° Generates initial KV cache entries for all prompt tokens\n\n        ° Latency proportional to prompt length\n\n        ° Benefits from larger batch sizes\n\n\n        ==>  Each new token depends on all the previous tokens, but because the full extent\n              of the input is known, at a high level this is a matrix-matrix operation that’s \n              highly parallelized.\n\n        ==> It effectively saturates GPU utilization",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1793530194714,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Vr-RMG5eXHqOVPKmsyCxb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 80.28358556138971,
      "y": 18259.804170409374,
      "width": 2534.39990234375,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#2f9e44",
      "backgroundColor": "#b2f2bb",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "dotted",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "iawWWCZovYvlboldb0hq2",
        "KYDunAKVG9xsZIgBFzSG7"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0Ad",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1637209491,
      "version": 178,
      "versionNonce": 1895430748,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793701873306,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2025/10/30/why-vllm-best-choice-ai-inference-today#better_memory_management_with_kv_cache",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "https://developers.redhat.com/articles/2025/10/30/why-vllm-best-choice-ai-inference-today#better_memory_management_with_kv_cache",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1793530194714,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
    {
      "id": "tOzjLUx4ZtSLUseKJPaqa",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 100.28358556138971,
      "y": 20179.804170409374,
      "width": 1499.7332763671875,
      "height": 1440,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "sSXcIa1jtrSpCXG4-Wdd-",
        "iawWWCZovYvlboldb0hq2",
        "KYDunAKVG9xsZIgBFzSG7"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "c0Ae",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2047585075,
      "version": 750,
      "versionNonce": 796813668,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793701873306,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "--> Decode phase ( token generation ) :\n\n        ° For each new token, reads ALL previous K and V values from cache\n\n        ° Stores both in Cache\n\n\n        ° Generates one token at a time, sequentially\n\n        ° Memory-bandwidth bound operation\n    \n        ° Reads the entire KV cache for each new token\n\n        ° Latency proportional to number of output tokens\n\n        ° Benefits from efficient cache management\n\n\n        ==> In the decode phase, the LLM generates output tokens autoregressively \n             one at a time, until a stopping criteria is met\n\n        ==>  Each sequential output token needs to know all the previous iterations’ \n              output states (keys and values). \n\n        ==> This is like a matrix-vector operation that underutilizes the GPU compute\n              ability compared to the prefill phase. \n\n        ==> The speed at which the data (weights, keys, values, activations) is \n              transferred to the GPU from memory dominates the latency, not how \n              fast the computation actually happens. \n\n        ==> In other words, this is a memory-bound operation.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "--> Decode phase ( token generation ) :\n\n        ° For each new token, reads ALL previous K and V values from cache\n\n        ° Stores both in Cache\n\n\n        ° Generates one token at a time, sequentially\n\n        ° Memory-bandwidth bound operation\n    \n        ° Reads the entire KV cache for each new token\n\n        ° Latency proportional to number of output tokens\n\n        ° Benefits from efficient cache management\n\n\n        ==> In the decode phase, the LLM generates output tokens autoregressively \n             one at a time, until a stopping criteria is met\n\n        ==>  Each sequential output token needs to know all the previous iterations’ \n              output states (keys and values). \n\n        ==> This is like a matrix-vector operation that underutilizes the GPU compute\n              ability compared to the prefill phase. \n\n        ==> The speed at which the data (weights, keys, values, activations) is \n              transferred to the GPU from memory dominates the latency, not how \n              fast the computation actually happens. \n\n        ==> In other words, this is a memory-bound operation.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "created": 1793530194714,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
